  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through Friday) \nIssued at 110 AM MDT Sat Sep 19 2026\n\nAnother very impressive surge of monsoon moisture is forecast to\nproduce widespread rainfall over the forecast area Tuesday\nafternoon through Friday. Rich subtropical moisture will again be\ndrawn northward Tuesday and Wednesday as the aforementioned CA \nlow pressure system tracks slowly east northeastward over the \nnorthern and central Rockies, while a mid-level high pressure \nsystem parks over eastern TX. During the latter half of the work\nweek, the high is forecast to remain in place while drawing \nadditional monsoon moisture and embedded disturbances northward \nover NM. At this time, periods of locally locally heavy rainfall \nlook to favor all but the Four Corners Tuesday through Friday,\nwith precip totals elsewhere during the work week potentially \nreaching 1-3 inches; with locally higher amounts over 4 inches. \nModels vary on whether a tropical storm in the eastern Pacific \nwill enhance precipitation over the forecast area Thursday night \nand Friday. The operational run of the ECMWF brings the remnant \nmoisture over much of NM, but the operational runs of the GFS and \nCanadian Models keep the tropical storm over the Pacific. The\ndeciding factor could be how deeply an incoming storm system digs\noff the western US coast, since the latest ECMWF deepens the\nupper low significantly more than the GFS and drops it \nsignificantly farther south.",
